# {{ .prefix }}-bugfix

The fix-and-verify task skill.{{ if .skills.debugging }} Companion to `{{ .prefix }}-debugging`: where debugging owns systematic investigation (finding the root cause), this skill owns the implementation + review pair that ships the fix.{{ end }}

<!-- awf:include durable-oracle -->

## When to invoke

When the root cause is known and a fix is ready to land. Two callers in practice:

- **Trivial bugfix that validly skips the chain**: the narrow exception in `{{ .layout.workflowRef }}` for a locally obvious, directly verified fix. This skill is the entire flow.
- **Bugfix with upstream design work**: preserve the approved design boundary while implementing and independently evaluate continuity and review need.

{{ if .skills.debugging }}If the root cause is not yet known, invoke `{{ .prefix }}-debugging` first.{{ else }}If the root cause is not yet known, confirm it with a falsifiable check before touching code.{{ end }}

## Procedure

<!-- awf:include outline-approval -->

This skill may run without an effort. If continuity materially helps, invoke `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` before mutation; if an effort exists, validate its fixed identity and exact `.awf/efforts/<slug>/memory.md`, preserve one writer, and give children that context read-only. Otherwise omit effort and memory fields. {{if eq .profile "core"}}Project documentation, source, tests, and repository history remain authoritative{{else}}Repository sources and current-state documentation remain authoritative{{end}}, and standalone memory is forbidden.

1. **Establish the oracle before the fix.** Select evidence under the durable-oracle rule above and record any concrete reason the preferred automated red-then-green path is impractical. {{ if .skills.tdd }}Invoke `{{ .prefix }}-tdd` to establish and exercise that evidence before implementation.{{ else }}Exercise the selected evidence against the unfixed behaviour before implementation.{{ end }} {{if eq .profile "core"}}First inspect the implementation and verification paths.{{else}}First run `./awf context <the implementation and verification paths>`.{{end}}
<!-- awf:include context-orientation -->
<!-- awf:include context-spill -->

2. **Implement the root-cause fix, not the symptom.** Per `{{ .layout.maintainableCodeDesign }}`, assess whether the root cause is an unsuitable model or boundary; include bounded enabling work that prevents a workaround.
<!-- awf:include clean-integration -->
<!-- awf:include implementation-autonomy -->
For materially larger work, route the disposition through {{ if .skills.brainstorming }}`{{ .prefix }}-brainstorming`{{ else }}the active workflow's design discussion{{ end }}:
<!-- awf:include escalation-menu -->
No safety bypasses. Repair defects caused by this transaction or blocking safe completion; record and route unrelated concrete defects separately without expanding scope. No incidental refactors riding along; one concern per commit. No speculative shims.

<!-- awf:section pitfalls-check -->
{{ if .layout.docs.pitfalls }}   Before writing the fix, read the compact generated pitfall index at `{{ .layout.docs.pitfalls }}`, then open only relevant linked leaves for known-tricky areas; verify the fix is not re-introducing one that bit before.
{{ end }}<!-- awf:end -->

3. **Verify via the gates.** {{ with .vars.gateCmd }}`{{ . }}`{{ else }}The project's gate{{ end }} is the default.{{ if .vars.gateCmdFull }} Run `{{ .vars.gateCmdFull }}` when regression-test placement warrants the full tier.{{ end }}

4. **Commit** with Conventional Commits, typically `fix(<scope>): ...`; the body explains the *why*. Retain the selected durable evidence and, when it is not the preferred automated path, its concrete reason.

5. **Evaluate implementation review independently.** Invoke {{ if index .skills "reviewing-impl" }}`{{ .prefix }}-reviewing-impl`{{ else }}the project's review step{{ end }} for meaningful breadth, non-obvious logic, contract or compatibility effects, migration or high-consequence risk, substantive verification judgment, or uncertainty. Skip only locally obvious, low-risk, directly verified work. Effort-backed work returns to `{{ if index .skills "effort-workflow" }}{{ .prefix }}-effort-workflow{{ else }}the effort lifecycle owner{{ end }}` after review settles or is explicitly skipped.

